WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.610
- We are back here with
actor-extraordinaire,

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:06.240
but also a "Bachelor" superfan,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.970
Topher Grace, everybody!

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.660
- I'm happy to-
(audience cheering)

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.670
I'm happy to say, Jesse asked me,

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.902
and I am going to be the next "Bachelor"!

00:00:13.902 --> 00:00:14.873
(Drew cheering)
(Jesse cheering)

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:17.010
Yes!
(audience cheering)

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.823
Wow! I can't believe it!

00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:23.590
- But also, the extraordinary
host of "The Bachelor",

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.926
Jesse Palmer is here.
- Thank you so much

00:00:25.926 --> 00:00:26.759
for having me.
(audience cheering)

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.720
Thank you.
- Gracing us, pun intended,

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.160
with his presence.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.250
Okay, what is your favorite part

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.946
about hosting "The Bachelor"?

00:00:35.946 --> 00:00:39.410
- Well, it's way less
stressful being the host

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.880
than it is actually being "The Bachelor",

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.000
because you don't have to worry about

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.840
dealing with all the drama.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.750
You don't have to deal with
breaking people's hearts,

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.010
calling out the wrong
name at rose ceremonies.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.581
Like somebody once upon a time did.

00:00:51.581 --> 00:00:52.582
(audience laughing)

00:00:52.582 --> 00:00:56.670
- I cannot imagine what it's
like to be "The Bachelor".

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:57.840
I really can't.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.840
Jesse, do you think that
we even ask a bachelor?

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.640
'Cause we do have another
surprise for Topher.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:06.500
- We do, listen,
- What's going on?

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.320
- I mean, obviously, I was "The Bachelor".

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.870
It was a long time ago.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:11.560
You were probably just
a kid when it happened

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.540
but there is someone

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.700
I can think of.
- Who?

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.040
- A certain Mr. Clayton Echard
- You would.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.527
- Maybe, everybody?
- Yes.

00:01:18.527 --> 00:01:20.392
- "The Bachelor" now,
- The actual-

00:01:20.392 --> 00:01:21.614
- Clayton Echard, there he is!

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.565
(Drew cheering)
(audience cheering)

00:01:23.565 --> 00:01:25.495
(Drew screaming)
(audience cheering)

00:01:25.495 --> 00:01:27.611
- Clayton Echard,
- Topher.

00:01:27.611 --> 00:01:28.623
- You're here!
- Topher, Drew,

00:01:28.623 --> 00:01:30.870
yeah, Jesse.
- You know, Drew thinks

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:31.780
this is a prank on me,

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.668
but this is actually
just a prank on my wife.

00:01:33.668 --> 00:01:35.100
(Jesse laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.691
- Well, I was gonna say Ashley Grace,

00:01:36.691 --> 00:01:39.010
how you doing?
(Drew screaming)

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.850
I wanna shout her out as well.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.610
- Oh man, Clayton, just
give us a hint, man.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:44.710
Give us a hint.
(Drew inhaling sharply)

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.190
- Do you want me to wink
one time if this happened,

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:50.550
or wink twice for another?
(Topher laughing)

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.060
Listen, I'm doing well overall.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:56.110
I heard you said you hadn't
seen "The Women Tell All".

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.160
Buckle up for that one.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.190
I had to do that, to say the least.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:02.390
- Are you very happy
in your life right now?

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.050
- I am a happy man.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:05.883
Yes.
- Yeah? Okay.

00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:06.810
I've learned a lot of lessons,

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.100
and I'm better than I was when
I came in, as a human being.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.770
- Clayton for you,
having been a "Bachelor",

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:18.850
and now that, or being on both
sides of it, I should say,

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:22.680
what do you like best about
being in the driver's seat?

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.633
And what's the worst thing about it?

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.420
- Oh, Jesse alluded to it. I'll start off.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.450
I always wanna end on a good note,

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:29.810
so let me start off with what was tough,

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:33.610
was the lack of control.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:34.470
I had a little bit,

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.820
but not nearly as much as
what I thought at times,

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.147
and I had to be able to sit back

00:02:38.147 --> 00:02:40.710
and just tell myself, "Hey,
roll with the punches.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.090
Do what you can. Be your authentic self.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.130
And at the end of the day, if you do that,

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:47.660
you won't look back and have regrets".

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:48.780
Even though I made mistakes,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.180
I mean, it's so very
apparent as everyone's seen,

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.990
and I accept full responsibility
for those actions.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.932
But with that, again, I
think the best part about it

00:02:56.932 --> 00:02:59.840
is I've been able to
grow as an individual.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.040
I think I had five years of growth

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.300
that packed into two months,

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.220
and for that I'm so very thankful.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.180
I built so many great connections,

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.400
and for that, again,
it's like I'm just happy

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.520
to have been able to go through it.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.200
- I'd love to ask
(audience applauding)

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.653
Clayton, Jesse, and Topher,

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:24.530
as a woman, if I could
hear your deal breakers,

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.940
what is one thing you cannot
live without in a woman?

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:31.830
What is one thing you
can't live with a woman?

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.603
Clayton, you start please.

00:03:34.999 --> 00:03:37.990
- (sighs) Sense of humor is
right there up at the top.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:39.260
So I look for somebody that can make me

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:42.610
laugh on a daily basis, and
someone that's a little weird.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:43.443
I like weirdness.

00:03:43.443 --> 00:03:45.040
It just makes me, it's unique,

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.500
and keeps me on my toes.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:48.690
So that's something I look for.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.600
Something that frustrates me,

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.060
is, it's kind of just, I think,

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.520
what everybody else would say,

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:59.165
as far as someone who's rude or impatient,

00:03:59.165 --> 00:04:00.900
something along those lines.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.430
I think I just want someone
who's understanding,

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.595
and that's critical
more than anything else.

00:04:05.595 --> 00:04:07.483
- Okay. Good to know.
(audience applauding)

00:04:07.483 --> 00:04:09.850
Good to know for the last three ladies.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:10.930
Jesse, what about you?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.220
What is a must have, and
what's a deal breaker?

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.030
- I'm real big on family values,

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.494
and it doesn't hurt if you
make great chocolate brownies.

00:04:17.494 --> 00:04:19.425
(audience laughing)

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:24.425
I think if, a deal breaker for me would be

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.720
if you were inconsiderate.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.810
I think for me, that that's a big one.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:29.880
That would probably be it for me.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:30.713
- You stole mine, dude.

00:04:30.713 --> 00:04:31.714
I would actually, I would,

00:04:31.714 --> 00:04:33.380
kind of the same thing as you.
- Brownies?

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.244
- Yeah, brownies.
- Oh.

00:04:34.244 --> 00:04:35.474
(Drew laughing)
(audience laughing)

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.980
- No, but I think, respect for others.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.320
- What is-
- I went on a date, early on,

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.890
where someone was really
rude to the waiter,

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:43.220
and I just thought like,
(Drew gasping)

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.067
but she was being really
nice to me, and I thought,

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.220
"That's not cool.
- No.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.806
This person's actually
serving us", you know?

00:04:47.806 --> 00:04:51.570
You gotta be, it was
a great telltale sign.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:53.483
- Yeah, and a must-have?

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.145
- Everything that Ashley
Grace is. (chuckles)

00:04:57.145 --> 00:04:58.270
(Jesse laughing)
(audience applauding)

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.010
- [Clayton] Smart man, smart man.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.947
- Jesse and Clayton, thank you so much

00:05:01.947 --> 00:05:03.544
- Of course, man.
- That was great.

00:05:03.544 --> 00:05:04.525
- for gracing us

00:05:04.525 --> 00:05:05.358
- Thank y'all so much.
- With your time

00:05:05.358 --> 00:05:06.191
and your presence.

00:05:06.191 --> 00:05:08.690
And Topher, your amazing
show, "Home Economics"

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:12.120
is every Wednesday night at 9:30 on ABC.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.130
Congratulations. It's a huge success.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:15.540
And I'm so happy for you,

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.110
because you deserve everything

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.220
good in your life
- And you too.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:19.720
- and you just put out the good,

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.564
and you are good, and this was so good.

00:05:22.564 --> 00:05:25.147
(bright music)

